Description: Estimation and analysis of allostatic load from biomarker panels.
    Protocols define biomarkers, physiological systems, risk directions and
    missing-data rules; references are fitted as pooled, stratified or
    age-conditional thresholds, or as means and standard deviations, and
    applied unchanged to new cohorts and visits. Scores include counts,
    proportions, z-scores and system-balanced indices. Analyses cover group
    decomposition, risk patterns, measurement and biological variation,
    calibration bootstrap, specification analysis, cross-validated
    comparison with outcomes, survey weights, multiple imputation, cohort
    harmonization, outlier detection and longitudinal models. Methods follow
    Seeman et al. (1997) <doi:10.1001/archinte.1997.00440400111013>.
